{"title":"2006 IMO Shortlist Problems/A4","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_IMO_Shortlist_Problems/A4&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Prove the inequality\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/a/d/5ad7bedff1e97d683345dcb2942d2aef77246574.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\sum_{i&lt;j} \\frac{a_ia_j}{a_i+a_j} \\le \\frac{n}{2(a_1 + a_2 + \\dotsb a_n)} \\sum_{i&lt;j} a_i a_j\\]\" width=\"321\" height=\"42\" />\nfor positive real numbers <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/0/8c0abca49eca38c071d36601233bd3bbbfd6c54d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_1, \\dotsc, a_n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"75\" height=\"11\" />.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution\">Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_IMO_Shortlist_Problems/A4&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Note that\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/1/d/81df70c470be92c39cecee7dec4d8e44b564bac1.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\sum_{i&lt;j} \\frac{a_ia_j}{a_i+a_j} = 1/2 \\sum_{i\\neq j} \\frac{a_ia_j}{a_i + a_j} = 1/2 \\sum_{j=1}^n \\sum_{i\\neq j} \\frac{1}{1/a_i + 1/a_j} .\\]\" width=\"437\" height=\"50\" />\nSuppose that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/2/7/b274192b0b23368dd6e1832bc846dd78d5030b0f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1 \\le k \\neq \\ell \\le n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"110\" height=\"17\" />.  Note that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/1/9/81911702f357752d15ed250aa571e8d2d9aaee27.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1/(1/a_i + 1/a_j)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -6px\" width=\"124\" height=\"20\" /> is an increasing function of both <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/2/412787c048e28774dc63fc27db42dc52ca858de7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_i$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"14\" height=\"10\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/7/8/0785f19824c8b23ab3dfe000b471994078fdf589.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_j$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"15\" height=\"12\" />.  It follows that if <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/6/6/566dfb426a6d4967924e98ad81182eebaf8cfef5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_k \\le a_\\ell$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"56\" height=\"15\" />, then\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/4/5/5457135c2a4cb283bfb9de2ab68894f6c37d7e32.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\sum_{j \\neq k} \\frac{1}{1/a_k + 1/a_j} \\le \\sum_{j\\neq \\ell} \\frac{1}{a_\\ell + a_j},\\]\" width=\"241\" height=\"47\" />\ni.e., <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/a/0/fa0dd75b31ddfbfbbe55cf28687a5fd0a10bd95d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\sum_{j\\neq i} \\frac{1}{1/a_i + 1/a_j}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -23px\" width=\"121\" height=\"47\" /> is an increasing function of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/1/2/8122aa89ea6e80784c6513d22787ad86e36ad0cc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$j$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"10\" height=\"17\" />.\n</p><p>Since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/5/8/f58bf13a012a12e556086c3fb68aa668244936e9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\sum_{i\\neq j}(a_j + a_i) = (n-2)a_j + \\sum_{i=1}^n a_i$\" style=\"vertical-align: -23px\" width=\"256\" height=\"50\" /> is also an increasing function of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/1/2/8122aa89ea6e80784c6513d22787ad86e36ad0cc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$j$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"10\" height=\"17\" />, it follows from <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Chebyshev%27s_Inequality\" title=\"Chebyshev&#39;s Inequality\">Chebyshev's Inequality</a> that\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/b/2/db2f635ea17282bd3b0be9606b5f31cc254dc572.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\frac{2n-2}{n} \\sum_{j=1}^n a_j \\cdot \\sum_{j=1}^n \\sum_{j\\neq i} \\frac{1}{1/a_i + 1/a_j} \\le \\sum_{j=1}^n \\left[ \\sum_{i\\neq j} (a_i + a_j) \\cdot \\sum_{i\\neq j} \\frac{1}{1/a_i + 1/a_j} \\right],\\]\" width=\"569\" height=\"55\" />\nor\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/6/5/c65ec022e65e514ce242f2ccac661d793dae3bb5.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[1/2 \\sum_{j=1}^n a_j \\cdot \\sum_{j=1}^n \\sum_{j\\neq i} \\frac{1}{1/a_i + 1/a_j} \\le \\frac{n}{4(n-1)} \\sum_{j=1}^n \\left[ \\sum_{i\\neq j} (a_i + a_j) \\cdot \\sum_{i\\neq j} \\frac{1}{1/a_i + 1/a_j} \\right] .\\]\" width=\"613\" height=\"55\" />\nNow, for fixed <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/1/2/8122aa89ea6e80784c6513d22787ad86e36ad0cc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$j$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"10\" height=\"17\" />, both <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/7/8/3782a4378501050057942516f6257eb718fa9386.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_i + a_j$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"52\" height=\"15\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/1/9/81911702f357752d15ed250aa571e8d2d9aaee27.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1/(1/a_i + 1/a_j)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -6px\" width=\"124\" height=\"20\" /> are increasing functions of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/2/412787c048e28774dc63fc27db42dc52ca858de7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_i$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"14\" height=\"10\" />.  It follows again from Chebyshev's Inequality that\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/2/b/a2b0dd20c4acc64f6198550bbc16ed451d0a9fbf.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\frac{1}{n-1} \\sum_{i\\neq j} (a_i + a_j) \\sum_{i \\neq j} \\frac{1}{1/a_i + 1/a_j} \\le \\sum_{i\\neq j} \\frac{a_i+a_j}{1/a_i + 1/a_j} = \\sum_{i\\neq j} a_i a_j,\\]\" width=\"503\" height=\"47\" />\nor\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/c/2/fc2e0aa3e69b4d3ff87fddbe94d23df3a3cbe823.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\sum_{i\\neq j} (a_i + a_j) \\sum_{i \\neq j} \\frac{1}{1/a_i + 1/a_j} \\le (n-1) \\sum_{i\\neq j} a_ia_j,\\]\" width=\"367\" height=\"47\" />\nwhich in sum becomes\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/b/c/8bc707084f9f77b84bb19eef1580f023000ea44d.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\frac{n}{4(n-1)} \\sum_{j=1}^n \\left[ \\sum_{i\\neq j}(a_i + a_j) \\sum_{i \\neq j} \\frac{1}{1/a_i + 1/a_j} \\right] \\le \\frac{n}{4} \\sum_{j=1}^n \\sum_{i \\neq j} a_i a_j = \\frac{n}{2} \\sum_{i&lt;j} a_i a_j .\\]\" width=\"577\" height=\"55\" />\nIf we denote <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/8/5/8857f0c8fb7dea08640e400e0fe2519d09e1bb25.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\sum_{i=1}^n a_i =S$\" style=\"vertical-align: -20px\" width=\"80\" height=\"48\" />, then in summary, we thus have\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/7/0/b702ebb3a606df76c6d165735c567fab7b2c9fce.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\sum_{i &lt; j} \\frac{a_ia_j}{a_i + a_j} = (1/S) \\cdot S/2 \\cdot \\sum_{j=1}^n \\sum_{i\\neq j} \\frac{1}{1/a_i + 1/a_j} \\le n/(2S) \\cdot \\sum_{i&lt;j} a_i a_j,\\]\" width=\"495\" height=\"50\" />\nas desired.  <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/b/b/3bbb9e25e5be095e317771a9c5d00877ee9c8012.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\blacksquare$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" />\n</p><p><br />\n<i>Alternate solutions are always welcome. If you have a different, elegant solution to this problem, please <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/index.php?title=2006_IMO_Shortlist_Problems/A4&amp;action=edit\">add it</a> to this page.</i>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Resources\">Resources</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_IMO_Shortlist_Problems/A4&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Resources\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<ul><li><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_IMO_Shortlist_Problems\" title=\"2006 IMO Shortlist Problems\">2006 IMO Shortlist Problems</a></li>\n<li><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"http://www.mathlinks.ro/Forum/viewtopic.php?p=874975#p874975\">Discussion on AoPS/MathLinks</a></li></ul>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261018052451\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: []\nCPU time usage: 0.017 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.029 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 141/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 353/2097152 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 0/2097152 bytes\nHighest expansion depth: 4/100\nExpensive parser function count: 0/100\nUnstrip recursion depth: 0/20\nUnstrip post‐expand size: 5650/5000000 bytes\n-->\n<!--\nTransclusion expansion time report (%,ms,calls,template)\n100.00%    5.955      1 Template:Alternate_solutions\n100.00%    5.955      1 -total\n-->\n\n<!-- Saved in parser cache with key wiki-wiki_:pcache:6094:|#|:idhash:canonical and timestamp 20261018052451 and revision id 21664. Rendering was triggered because: api-parse\n -->\n</div>"}